  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_gRH7AJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_gUdi4JXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="LatencyAnalysis checks the latency (finishTime - releaseTime) for each&#xA;release of each flow for the WARP system. To be correct, the latency must be&#xA;less than or equal than the flows deadline parameter.&#xA;&#xA;@author sgoddard&#xA;@version 1.6" item="_dq_VqWYXEe6uL7xt-YnTxg">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH01EJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_gdGhgJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_gf9BMJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="Get the latencyReport build by buildLatencyReport().&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * @return latencyReport" item="_dq_V1mYXEe6uL7xt-YnTxg">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH1cIZXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_grxPoJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_guoWYJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="Counts the number of push/pull instructions in the instruction string (input&#xA;&#x9; * parameter) whose flow, src, and snk parameters match the input parameters.&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * @param flow  name of the flow to match&#xA;&#x9; * @param src   source node of the instruction to match&#xA;&#x9; * @param snk   sink node of the instruction to match&#xA;&#x9; * @param instr string containing the instructions to be searched for matches&#xA;&#x9; * @return numTx the number of matching push/pull instructions" item="_dq_V22YXEe6uL7xt-YnTxg">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH2DMZXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_g0ft0JXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_g2790JXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="Constructor for warp objects. Both constructors do the same thing.&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * @param warp Object providing an interface to the program to be analyzed." item="_dq_V7GYXEe6uL7xt-YnTxg">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH01EZXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_g_UdwJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_hB0_MJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="Constructor that program objects. Both constructors do the same thing, but&#xA;&#x9; * this constructor can be called by an object that doesn't have access to the&#xA;&#x9; * parent Warp object.&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * @param program Warp program to be analyzed" item="_dq_V9WYXEe6uL7xt-YnTxg">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH1cIJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_hH380JXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_hKX3MJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="Build a latency report. Flows are output in priority order (based on the&#xA;&#x9; * priority used to build the program. The latency for each instance of the flow&#xA;&#x9; * is reported as follows &quot;Maximum latency for FlowName:Instance is Latency&quot;&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * For flow instances that have latency > deadline, then the latency message is&#xA;&#x9; * appended with the string &quot; => DEADLINE MISS&quot;&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * A line of 30 '*' characters separates each group of flow instance reports.&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * When there are not enough transmissions attempted between the release and the&#xA;&#x9; * next release of an instance, then the latency is not computed (as we assume&#xA;&#x9; * deadline less than or equal to the period. Thus, the report is: &quot;UNKNOWN&#xA;&#x9; * latency for FlowName:Instance; Not enough transmissions attempted&quot;.&#xA;&#x9; *" item="_zk4lYHLhEe6TWvrCv_9N1A">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH1cIpXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_hQMLUJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_hSpCYJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="Adds the {@link #FLOW_SEPARATOR FLOW_SEPARATOR} line to the latencyReport." item="_faiRQJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH2DMJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_hYvDUJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_hbL6YJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="Computer and report the latency incurred for each release of Flow flowName.&#xA;&#x9; * This method finds the flow's source and sink nodes. It also gets the number&#xA;&#x9; * of transmission attempts required for last link in the flow. Then it loops&#xA;&#x9; * through the hyperperiod calling the&#xA;&#x9; * {@link #computeAndRecordFlowInstanceLatency(Integer, String, Integer, String, Integer, String, Integer, Integer)&#xA;&#x9; * computeAndRecordFlowInstanceLatency} method to get the actual number of&#xA;&#x9; * attempts made for each instance of the flow before its next release. If the&#xA;&#x9; * number of attempts is less than that required, the deadline was missed and&#xA;&#x9; * recorded by {@link #recordMissedDeadline(String, Integer, Integer)&#xA;&#x9; * recordMissedDeadline}. A flow separation line is printed out after each&#xA;&#x9; * instance's latency is reported.&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * @param flowName for which the latency of each instance will reported" item="_fa754JXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH1cI5XmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_hvmEIJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_hyeZAJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="Computes the latency for the specified instance of the flow and calls&#xA;&#x9; * {@link #recordLatency(String, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer)&#xA;&#x9; * recordLatency} to record the latency if all numTxRequired transmission&#xA;&#x9; * attempts complete before the next release. The number of transmission&#xA;&#x9; * attempts made before the next release is returned.&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * @param time          the current time slot&#xA;&#x9; * @param flowName      flow to be analyzed&#xA;&#x9; * @param instance      instance of the flow to be analyzed&#xA;&#x9; * @param src           source node of the instruction being analyzed&#xA;&#x9; * @param srcIndex      column index of the program table for the source node&#xA;&#x9; * @param snk           sink node of the instruction being analyzed&#xA;&#x9; * @param snkIndex      column index of the program table for the sink node&#xA;&#x9; * @param numTxRequired number of transmission attempts required&#xA;&#x9; * @return" item="_fbUUYJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH1cJJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_iBMxgJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_iDvIIJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="Evaluates the latency based on input parameters and records the maximum&#xA;&#x9; * latency encountered or a deadline miss, as appropriate, in the latencyReport.&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * @param flowName    flow for which the latency is being recorded&#xA;&#x9; * @param time        of the last push/pull instruction for this instance of the&#xA;&#x9; *                    flow&#xA;&#x9; * @param releaseTime time when this instance of the flow was released&#xA;&#x9; * @param deadline    time which this instance of the flow must be completed&#xA;&#x9; * @param instance    the number of times (-1) the flow has been released (1st&#xA;&#x9; *                    release is instance 0)" item="_fcGXgZXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH1cJZXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_iRyLMJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_iUqgEJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="Adds an UNKNOWN latency report to the latencyReport when not enough&#xA;&#x9; * transmission attempts were made before the next release of the flow.&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * @param flowName flow for which the deadline miss is being recorded&#xA;&#x9; * @param instance instance number for the flow that missed its deadline&#xA;&#x9; * @param deadline time which this instance of the flow was to have been&#xA;&#x9; *                 completed" item="_fcojAJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH1cJpXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_ifVfAJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_iiQ3MJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="Checks if a flow has no pushes, pulls, releases, or deadlines at a certain&#xA;&#x9; * time of an input flow.&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * @param flowName The string name of a flow which should be analyzed for if it&#xA;&#x9; *                 is idle.&#xA;&#x9; * @param timeslot An integer which corresponds to a timeslot in the schedule.&#xA;&#x9; * @return A boolean which should be true if there are no instructions,&#xA;&#x9; *         deadlines, or releases in the given timeslot of the given flow." item="_fdPnAJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH2DMpXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_itzY0JXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_it3DMJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="This method checks for each characteristic of a flow, and updates a latency&#xA;&#x9; * table entry corresponding to the given flow and timeslot with that&#xA;&#x9; * characteristic.&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * @param flowName The string name of a flow, used to access an entry in the&#xA;&#x9; *                 latency table.&#xA;&#x9; * @param timeslot An integer which corresponds to a timeslot in the schedule,&#xA;&#x9; *                 used to access an entry in the latency table.&#xA;&#x9; * @param value    A constant string that corresponds to the character&#xA;&#x9; *                 representing a characteristic of the flow." item="_ffKSkJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH2DM5XmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_i2Nt8JXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_i5FbwJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="This method checks if an instance of the flow is released and then updates an&#xA;&#x9; * entry corresponding to the given flow and timeslot in the latency table with&#xA;&#x9; * the RELEASE constant.&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * @param flowName The string name of a flow, used to update the latency table.&#xA;&#x9; * @param timeslot An integer which corresponds to a timeslot in the schedule,&#xA;&#x9; *                 used to update the latency table." item="_fgVXQJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH2DNJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_jBvogJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_jErnwJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="This method checks if the last instruction of the flow instance is released&#xA;&#x9; * and then updates an entry corresponding to the given flow and timeslot in the&#xA;&#x9; * latency table with the COMPLETE constant.&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * @param flowName The string name of a flow, used to update the latency table.&#xA;&#x9; * @param timeslot An integer which corresponds to a timeslot in the schedule,&#xA;&#x9; *                 used to update the latency table." item="_fhJPkZXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH2DNZXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_jPkpIJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_jSjrsJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="This method checks if there are push/pull instructions, and then updates an&#xA;&#x9; * entry in the latency table with the push/pull instruction symbol.&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * @param flowName The string name of a flow, used to update the latency table.&#xA;&#x9; * @param timeslot An integer which corresponds to a timeslot in the schedule,&#xA;&#x9; *                 used to update the latency table." item="_fhrbEZXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH2DNpXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_jbVNMJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_jeQlYJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="This method checks if there is an absolute deadline for the released flow&#xA;&#x9; * instance then updates an entry corresponding to the given flow and timeslot&#xA;&#x9; * in the latency table with the DEADLINE constant.&#xA;&#x9; * &#xA;&#x9; * @param flowName The string name of a flow, used to update the latency table.&#xA;&#x9; * @param timeslot An integer which corresponds to a timeslot in the schedule,&#xA;&#x9; *                 used to update the latency table." item="_fiViYJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH2DN5XmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_jpaFcJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_jsMTsJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="&#xA;  &#x9; * &#xA;  &#x9; * @param flowName The string name of a flow&#xA;  &#x9; * @param instr A string corresponding to an entry to programTable that describes an instruction at a timeslot.&#xA;  &#x9; * @return" item="_fi48AZXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH2DOJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_kBCiUJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_kD8FUJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="This method creates a title using the name of the workload to be used as the graph name. It should be private since it is only called&#xA;  * within this file, but it is public so that we can create tests for this helper method.&#xA;  *&#xA;  * Return: A formatted string that includes the name of the workload as the graph name.&#xA;  *" item="_kGXHMJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH2DOpXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_kMar4JXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_kPUO4JXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="LatencyVisualization creates the visualizations for the liability analysis of the WARP program.&#xA;&lt;p>&#xA;&#xA;CS2820 Fall 2023 Project: Implement this class to create the file visualization that is&#xA;requested in Warp.&#xA;&#xA;@author sgoddard&#xA;@version 1.6&#xA; *" item="_drym7GYXEe6uL7xt-YnTxg">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_gH2DOZXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_rzTkwJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_r1rjUJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="@author sgoddard&#xA; *">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_rwBANZXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_r9A6YJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_r92n4JXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="Returns the Workload object used to build the program&#xA;   * &#xA;   * @return WorkLoad object containing a graph, flows, and&#xA;   * nodes that this program's schedule was generated for.">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_rwBANpXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_sDIwgJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_sFeS0JXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="Returns the program schedule that was built.&#xA;   * &#xA;   * @return&#x9;Program schedule object containing the instructions.">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_rwBAN5XmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_sLwhAJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_sLwhAZXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="Creates a map from the node names to index locations in the schedule table.&#xA;   * &#xA;   * @return HashMap that maps node names to their index in the schedule table.">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_rwBAOJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_sWvB8JXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_sZ4ckJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="This class handles the code related to the VisualizationObject,&#xA;which is related to how the stress tests are visualized&#xA;@author sgoddard&#xA;@version 1.5&#xA; *" item="_gZC3WWYXEe6uL7xt-YnTxg">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_rwCOVpXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
  <nodes xsi:type="com.yattasolutions.diagrams:CommentVisual" xmi:id="_sl4RMJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" sourceConnectionVisual="_sov_AJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA" text="Another nameExtension method to deal with cases where there isn't a specific double m and double e2e&#xA;   * @param schName - String schName&#xA;   * @param numFaults - Integer numFaults&#xA;   * @return - Extension String" item="_gZC3dWYXEe6uL7xt-YnTxg">
    <modelElement href="Latency.uml#_rwCOXJXmEe6MhezhJ-iEDA"/>
  </nodes>
